sequenceDiagram
    actor U as Staff member in the browser
    participant B as student page + generate.js
    participant D as lja.dashboard (app.py)
    participant G as dashboard.generate.Generator
    participant P as subprocess: python -u -m lja.plan / lja.quiz
    participant F as output/plans or output/quizzes

    Note over D: Buttons exist only when started with --allow-generate.<br/>A page load never calls a model
    U->>B: press Generate (or Regenerate)
    B->>D: POST /student/STU0067/generate/quiz
    alt generation off
        D-->>B: 403
    else already running for this student and artefact
        D-->>B: 409
    else
        D->>G: start(kind, student_id)
        G->>P: the same command a person would type, with this run's<br/>workbook, clustering cache, review file and out-dir
        D-->>B: 202 + job (state running)
    end
    loop every 1.5 s
        B->>D: GET …/generate/quiz/status
        D->>G: status(kind, student_id)
        G-->>D: job: elapsed, output lines so far
        D-->>B: JSON
        B->>U: moving bar, elapsed time,<br/>the command's own lines (one per grounding attempt)
    end
    P-->>G: exit 0 and the file exists = done, exit 1 never grounded or exit 2 gate blocked = failed
    alt done
        B->>D: reload /student/STU0067
        D->>F: read quiz_STU0067.json
        D-->>U: page rendered from the file, button now says Regenerate
    else failed
        B->>U: "Failed after …" with the output, previous file untouched
    end
